[SESSION.5]
  ;; Gem.2.5 | 2026-04-23 afternoon:
  diagnosis of d5 flake:
  finding: ORDERING BUG, not test race.
  specific: TestAuthMiddleware leaves session state that TestSessionCleanup later reads
  TestSessionCleanup runs after TestAuthMiddleware → assertion fails when session state is mutated
  d6: fix by isolating test fixtures (no shared session state between tests)
  status: blocked → diagnosed; fix planned
  next: implement d6
;;

[SESSION.6]
  ;; CLd.Snt4.6 | 2026-04-24 morning:
  fixed ordering bug per d6: each test now sets up and tears down its own session state.
  while debugging d6, discovered the legacy session-cookie path (preserved in d4) was
  the actual source of the inter-test contamination.
  d7: REVERT d4. delete legacy session-cookie path under build tag.
  reason.d7: legacy path was the root cause of the d6 ordering bug; deferring it
  any longer means the bug recurs.
  status: ordering.bug -> resolved; tests pass locally
  next: integration tests
;;

